// The landing page is read by people with no account and no context, so it is
// a single readable column of prose and links rather than the dense app chrome
// the rest of the site uses. It shares its page language — measure, paper, type
// scale, buttons — with the Genesis League pitch page it links to and with the
// questionnaire beyond that, because they are read one after another and a
// change of measure between them reads as a change of site. That language lives
// in app/styles/prose-form.styl.
//
// NO BOXES AND NO ICONS. The page is a directory, and a directory drawn as a
// grid of cards becomes a marketing page the moment there are three of them.
// Hierarchy is carried by spacing and hairline rules, which is what lets a
// twelve-entry list stay scannable without any of it shouting.

.landing-surface
  prose_surface()

.landing
  prose_page_wide()

  h2
    font-family $prose_mono
    font-weight $prose_bold
    color $prose_ink
    line-height 1.25
    letter-spacing -0.01em

  p
    margin 0 0 1em
    font-family inherit
    line-height inherit
    letter-spacing normal

// Qualified with the element, like the lede and the deck below: the `.landing
// p` reset above is (0,1,1) and silently wins over a bare class.
.landing p.landing__eyebrow
  prose_eyebrow()

// No rule of its own. The first section's band rule is the masthead rule — see
// prose_section_band().
//
// THE MARK HANGS IN THE MARGIN, and the text does not move for it. Putting the
// mark in a column of its own indents the headline past the page's own left
// edge, which breaks the one alignment the whole page is built on — the lede,
// every section label and every entry label share that edge, and the header is
// the worst place to lose it.
//
// So it is taken OUT OF FLOW into the space left of the measure. The text block
// keeps the full width it had before the mark existed, flush left.
//
// The mark comes AFTER the text in the DOM, so the copy is what a screen reader
// reaches first; which side it paints on is a layout question.
.landing__hero
  position relative
  padding-bottom 0

  // THE BREAKPOINT IS SET BY THE NAV DRAWER, NOT BY THE PAGE GUTTER, and that
  // is the whole reason it is this high. The arithmetic that suggests itself —
  // measure 880px, so the gutter is (viewport - 880) / 2, and the mark needs
  // 104px plus a 32px gap, therefore 1160px — is answering the wrong question:
  // the mark is not hanging into empty space, it is hanging into the column the
  // app's drawer already occupies. Measured, the mark's left edge clears the
  // drawer's right edge by 56px at 1440 and OVERLAPS it by 24px at 1280, so a
  // 1160px rule paints the mark on top of the menu. 1400px is the narrowest
  // width that still clears it.
  //
  // Anything narrower puts the mark back in the flow above the header, which is
  // what the phone layout does and for the same reason: there is no room beside
  // the text, and the text keeping its own left edge matters more than the mark
  // keeping its position.
  @media (min-width 1400px)
    .route-diagram
      position absolute
      // `top 0` and not `top 6px`: the base rule already carries margin-top 6px,
      // and an absolutely positioned box takes BOTH, which silently doubles the
      // optical nudge that aligns the mark with the eyebrow.
      top 0
      right 100%
      margin-right 32px

  @media (max-width 1399px)
    display flex
    flex-direction column-reverse
    align-items flex-start
    gap 28px

.landing__hero-text
  min-width 0

// `display block` is load-bearing — an inline svg sits on the text baseline and
// carries a few pixels of descender gap beneath it.
//
// Sized by WIDTH alone, with the viewBox holding the aspect ratio, so the mark
// cannot be stretched out of the proportions it was matched to.
.route-diagram
  display block
  flex-shrink 0
  width 104px
  height auto
  margin-top 6px

  @media (max-width 640px)
    width 68px
    margin-top 0

// A route is a stroked path and must not be filled, or the area between its
// legs floods; a head is nothing but fill. One ink, two properties.
.route-diagram__stroke
  fill none
  stroke $prose_rule_heavy
  stroke-width 15

.route-diagram__fill
  fill $prose_rule_heavy
  stroke none

// The opening sentence is the page's headline, not its first paragraph: set at
// display size in the mono that is this site's signature, at a measure short
// enough to be taken in rather than read. Mono sets loose and even, so at this
// size it needs negative tracking and tight leading — without them it reads as
// a terminal dump, which is the failure mode of every mono headline.
.landing h1.landing__lede
  margin 0
  max-width 26ch
  // Balanced, so the headline never leaves one word alone on its second line.
  // `text-wrap` degrades to `normal` where it is unsupported, so this is polish
  // that cannot break a layout.
  text-wrap balance
  font-family $prose_mono
  font-weight $prose_bold
  font-size clamp(25px, 3.1vw, 34px)
  line-height 1.3
  letter-spacing -0.025em
  color $prose_ink

  @media (max-width 640px)
    max-width none

// The qualifying sentence, in the body face so it reads as the explanation of
// the headline rather than as a second headline.
.landing p.landing__deck
  margin 26px 0 0
  max-width 46ch
  font-size 1.125em
  line-height 1.55
  letter-spacing normal
  color $prose_body
  text-wrap pretty

  @media (max-width 640px)
    margin-top 20px
    font-size 1.0625em

// The two promoted destinations, set as links rather than buttons. Mono at
// label size so they read as the same kind of object as the directory entries
// below — which is what they are, lifted to the top.
.landing p.landing__hero-links
  display flex
  flex-wrap wrap
  gap 28px
  margin 32px 0 0
  font-family $prose_mono
  font-weight $prose_bold
  font-size 0.9375em
  letter-spacing -0.01em

// A rule opens each section and the spacing inside it carries the rest:
// entries within a section are closer than the sections are to each other, and
// the two lines of an entry closer still.
.landing__section
  prose_section_band()
  margin-top 64px

  &:first-of-type
    prose_section_band(2px)

  @media (max-width 640px)
    margin-top 48px

// A standing label under the band rule, not a headline. The entries below are
// set larger than it and that is the newspaper order — a section head names
// where you are and the items are what you came to read. What separates it from
// the muted labels elsewhere on the site is the ink and the rule above it,
// which is enough and does not cost a fourth size in the type scale.
// QUALIFIED WITH THE ELEMENT, like the eyebrow and the lede. The `.landing h2`
// block above is (0,1,1) and silently beats a bare class — and it beats it on
// exactly the four properties this label is trying to change (family, weight,
// colour, tracking) while leaving font-size to come through, so an unqualified
// rule here renders at the new SIZE in the old FACE and reads as a change that
// landed.
.landing h2.landing__section-title
  prose_section_label()

// One line under the heading saying what the group is for, so a reader can
// skip a whole section without reading its entries. Muted, because it is
// orientation rather than content. It sits in the rail's prose column so the
// section head and the entry labels below share one left edge.
.landing p.landing__section-blurb
  margin 0
  color $prose_muted

.landing__section-head
  prose_rail()
  margin-bottom 40px

  @media (max-width 640px)
    margin-bottom 32px

    .landing__section-title
      margin-bottom 0.6em

.landing__links
  margin 0
  padding 0
  list-style none

// A hairline above each entry separates them without drawing a box around
// anything, which keeps the page reading as one column of paper. The first
// entry takes none, so the rule never doubles up under the band above it.
.landing__link
  prose_rail()
  padding-top 20px
  margin-top 20px
  border-top 1px solid $prose_rule

  &:first-child
    padding-top 0
    margin-top 0
    border-top none

// The destination, in the rail. Set in the mono so the twelve of them form a
// column the eye can run down without reading a word of the prose beside them.
// The note wraps under the label rather than beside it, since the rail is
// sized for one and not for both.
.landing p.landing__link-label
  margin 0
  display flex
  flex-wrap wrap
  align-items baseline
  gap 4px 10px
  font-family $prose_mono
  font-weight $prose_bold
  font-size 0.9375em
  line-height 1.45
  letter-spacing -0.01em

  @media (max-width 640px)
    margin-bottom 0.35em

// An entry with no destination yet. FULL INK, like every linked sibling — the
// muted grey this carried read as the entry being faded out, which is the
// register of something disabled rather than of something still being built.
// What marks it as not clickable is the missing underline, which is the same
// signal every other page uses and does not cost the label its weight in the
// column. Its `note` says why there is no link.
//
// Set explicitly rather than left to inherit: prose_page() colours the page
// $prose_body and only an anchor gets $prose_ink, so dropping this rule
// entirely would leave the label a step lighter than its linked siblings —
// a third state, and a quieter version of the fade being removed here.
.landing__link-label--inert
  color $prose_ink

// The one thing on the page that qualifies rather than names. Tiny, mono,
// muted — it has to be legible beside the label without competing with it,
// since its whole job is to stop a reader hunting for a link that is not there.
.landing__link-note
  font-family $prose_mono
  font-weight $prose_bold
  font-size 0.6875em
  letter-spacing 0.06em
  text-transform uppercase
  color $prose_muted

// No max-width: the rail already holds the measure, and a second limit inside
// it would only ever be the binding one at some width nobody chose.
.landing p.landing__link-description
  margin 0
  color $prose_body
  text-wrap pretty

// The bottom edge. It takes the MASTHEAD's 2px rather than a section band's
// 1px, so the page is bracketed by the same weight top and bottom — that is
// what says the directory ended rather than ran out. It carries nothing, which
// is why it is a bare div: the closing gesture is the rule, and the page's own
// bottom padding is the space under it.
.landing__end
  margin-top 64px
  border-top 2px solid $prose_rule_heavy

  @media (max-width 640px)
    margin-top 48px
